      "message": "I think this last check can\u0027t pass in a 4KB process: remap_pfn_range() refuses a 4KB VMA that starts at a nonzero slice of a kernel page (p3s_remap_pfn_range_size() in mm/p3s/memory.h), so this mmap() at a 4KB offset fails with EINVAL.\n\nI ran these steps on a VM with QEMU\u0027s EDU device. On the current branch the whole-BAR mapping above fails as well, because pci_mmap_fits() counts the 4KB VMA in 4KB pages; aosp/4417637 fixes that, and with it the first two checks pass and only this one fails.\n\nWould it be OK to expect the refusal here instead, as for the other remap_pfn_range() users? Something like:\n\n\tksft_test_result(slice_mapping \u003d\u003d MAP_FAILED \u0026\u0026 errno \u003d\u003d EINVAL,\n\t\t\t \"refuse a mapping at a sub-page PCI BAR offset\\n\");",
